{"symbol":"HINDZINC","updated":"2026-09-20T05:11 UTC","source":"screener.in + yfinance","url":"https://www.screener.in/company/HINDZINC/consolidated/","name":"Hindustan Zinc Ltd","about":"Incorporated in 1966, Hindustan Zinc in Zinc-Lead and Silver business is world’s 2nd largest integrated Zinc producer and Hindustan Zinc is the 3rd largest silver producer globally with an annual capacity of 800MT . The company has a market share of ~75% of the growing Zinc market in India with its headquarters at Zinc City, Udaipur along with Zinc-Lead mines and smelting complexes spread across the state of Rajasthan. [1]","key_points":"Business Segments [1] a) Zinc, Lead and Silver (94% in Q1 FY27 vs 97% in Q1 FY26): [2] [3] The company is the world’s largest integrated zinc producer and is amongst the top 10 silver producers globally. It supplies to more than 40 countries and holds a market share of about 74% of the primary zinc market in India. Its portfolio supports key sectors like infrastructure, railways, mobility, power, renewable energy and digital technologies, with applications ranging from construction, automotive and batteries to solar PV, semiconductors, jewellery and emerging solutions like zinc-air batteries and water purification.","top":{"Market Cap":"2,51,829 Cr.","Current Price":"596","High / Low":"733 / 446","Stock P/E":"14.8","Book Value":"53.6","Dividend Yield":"1.85 %","ROCE":"69.5 %","ROE":"76.6 %","Face Value":"2.00"},"quarters":[["","Sep 2024","Dec 2024","Mar 2025","Jun 2025","Sep 2025","Dec 2025","Mar 2026","Jun 2026"],["Sales +","8,252","8,614","9,087","7,771","8,549","10,980","13,544","13,747"],["Expenses +","4,129","4,115","4,267","3,912","4,104","4,926","5,838","5,697"],["Operating Profit","4,123","4,499","4,820","3,859","4,445","6,054","7,706","8,050"],["OPM %","50%","52%","53%","50%","52%","55%","57%","59%"],["Other Income +","187","218","227","279","238","318","280","316"],["Interest","303","285","251","240","259","195","187","132"],["Depreciatio